{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"four point corner pin tracking four point corner pin tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","fileName":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"four point corner pin tracking four point corner pin tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","fileName":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking","heading":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Tracking four corners of a planar region lets a replacement image deform with that region rather than merely translate, rotate, or scale. A corner-pin transform maps the four replacement corners onto their tracked locations, so a screen or sign can appear to follow perspective changes. The tracks should correspond to the same physical plane; points at different depths can make the warp inconsistent. This is a more expressive image-space match than [[One-Point and Two-Point Tracking]], but it is still not a 3D camera solve.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"four point corner pin tracking four point corner pin tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","fileName":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Four-Point Corner Pin Tracking","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}